    "table_title": "Flow Chart for Laboratory Parameters, for Screening, IMP Administration + Post-Treatment Follow-up (Week -6 to Week 52)",
    "table_purpose": "Laboratory parameters and sampling schedule from screening through Week 52 (detail of Table 1 \"Blood & semen sampling\")",
    "page_start": 21,
    "page_end": 23,
    "notes": "Classification: subsidiary (open call D3). Column structure differs from Table 1: D0 0h is absent, D0 post IMP is split into 1h/2h/3h hour columns (4-6) and D1 carries a 24h timepoint; Table 1 row \"Blood & semen sampling (see Table 2)\" points here, so the table gives finer timing for that activity (taxonomy decision tree: not same columns, not anchor, finer timing -> subsidiary). Alternative domain. One printed table over doc pp.21-22 (header reprinted on p.22 as rows 19-22, left out); doc p.23 carries only footnotes e-l (no activity rows). L=1; data columns 2-13, column 13 = Additional Visits. Bold full-width bands \"Local Laboratory\" / \"Central Laboratory\" are group headers; the Central Laboratory group stays open across the page break to p.22 (no band reprinted). Two stray 14pt Arial \"I\" glyphs in the Hours row sit exactly on the vertical rules between 1h/2h/3h - rule fragments, not cell content, not transcribed."
  },
